    "body": "As someone who works for CDN with animation conversion feature: animated WebP is bad. We would prefer not to use it. \r\n\r\nThe animated WebP format has been designed to be conceptually similar to GIF, and work for the same use-cases that GIF does, but this made it inherit GIF's weaknesses. Content that makes GIF sizes balloon typically also compresses poorly in WebP. Both are especially inefficient for short video clips with camera motion — a use-case handled better even by ancient codecs like MPEG-1. WebP often fails to meaningfully reduce GIF file sizes, and _can even end up making files larger than GIF_. \r\n\r\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
