    "updated_at": "2021-10-02T07:31:49Z",
    "body": "A concern I have about the current Chrome approach of allowing AV1 wrapped in AVIF in an img tag, but not AV1 wrapped in any other container, is the following:\r\n\r\nWhat about Nokia's patent claims on HEIF? AV1 is designed to be royalty-free, but the HEIF container that AVIF uses may not actually be royalty-free — at least Nokia does not give a patent grant, except for non-commercial purposes. See also: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=19874121\r\n\r\nIf we could use AV1 in any video container (in particular, in a non-patent-encumbered one), and not be forced to wrap it specifically in AVIF (which is based on HEIF), I would consider that a lot safer regarding potential patent trolling when adoption becomes larger and Nokia smells money. It would make perfect sense for them to lay low now and wait for more adoption before they start demanding royalties. These patents will only expire around 2035-2036, so they could be a problem.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
